WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.969
The gastrointestinal wall is an immune interface, with

00:00:04.969 --> 00:00:09.387
specialised barriers and molecular signals operating beside digestion.

00:00:13.008 --> 00:00:17.316
The immune system must distinguish threats from food-associated

00:00:17.316 --> 00:00:21.625
and resident signals. Breakdown can produce complex pathology.

00:00:25.175 --> 00:00:31.278
The chapter examines autoimmune gastrointestinal diseases and their aetiology, considering

00:00:31.278 --> 00:00:37.382
immunological mechanisms rather than treating all inflammation as one diagnosis.

00:00:41.967 --> 00:00:47.531
Histological patterns, molecular mechanisms and clinical presentation require careful

00:00:47.531 --> 00:00:53.095
reconciliation before attributing symptoms to a particular immune disorder.

00:00:57.342 --> 00:01:01.053
Mechanistic plausibility should be weighed against

00:01:01.053 --> 00:01:04.764
measured evidence and disease-specific diagnostic criteria.

00:01:07.883 --> 00:01:13.939
Part One of the 2022 open-access chapter explores what researchers

00:01:13.939 --> 00:01:19.994
understand about disease origins and pathophysiology, not a universal diagnosis.
